@startuml activity-fr-18-tools
' Report §2.1 — FR-18, the six tools the support agent may call (detail of activity-fr-18.puml).
' Source: SupportTools (six @Tool methods and the ownership guard), RefundGuard,
' RestRegistrationClient, RestPaymentClient, RestTicketingClient, UpstreamResults,
' InMemoryEscalationStore.
!include include/style.iuml
!include include/activity.iuml

title FR-18 — The support agent's tools (one tool call)

|concierge-service|
start
:the model requests one tool call
(SupportTools bound to the attendee from the request);
switch (tool requested)
case (listMyRegistrations)
  :registration-service:
  GET /api/v1/attendees/{attendeeId}/registrations
  (the request's attendee, never the model's);
case (lookupRegistration\nlookupTickets\nevaluateRefundPolicy)
  :ownership guard — registration-service:
  GET /api/v1/registrations/{id};
  if (held by this attendee?) then (no, or not found)
    :the same "not held by you" answer
    for a foreign id and a missing one;
  elseif (registration unreachable?) then (yes)
    :"service unavailable — offer escalation"
    (fails closed);
  else (yes)
    :the registration's details, or
    ticketing-service: GET
    /api/v1/registrations/{id}/tickets, or
    payment-service: GET
    /api/v1/refund-policy/quote, and
    whether requestRefund could approve it;
  endif
case (requestRefund)
  :guarded by RefundGuard and the
  200.00 AUD limit — see
  activity-fr-18-refund.puml;
case (escalateToOrganiser)
  if (already escalated in this conversation?) then (yes)
    :return the existing reference;
  else (no)
    :attach the registration only
    if verified
    as the attendee's —
    InMemoryEscalationStore.open
    with the model's summary <b>and</b> the
    attendee's own words;
  endif
endswitch

:the result is returned to the model;
stop

note right
  <b>Every guarantee is code, not prompt.</b>
  The attendee is bound from the HTTP request;
  the refund limit is checked inside requestRefund
  on a quote the tool fetched itself.
end note
@enduml
